<title>USA: Commodore IPO fell on first trade day.</title>
<headline>Commodore IPO fell on first trade day.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commodore Separation Technologies Inc closed at 4-1/8 on its first day of trading on Friday after the initial public offering of 1.5 million shares priced at $5.</p>
<p>National Securities was the lead underwriter for the deal.  </p>
<p>The warrants, however, which sold for $0.10 each in the IPO, rose to close at 1-3/4 on Friday.</p>
